# Tracer: forall free parameters inside function-space binders.
# Before (same code): the checked outer claim could not be reused by the
# template; selected_functions failed membership in power_set(fn(x X) X).
# Now: signature matching proposes the free X binding; complete strict alpha
# equality still checks the carrier, guards, return set and bound occurrences.
# Boundary: mismatched arity/return carriers and escaped local binders remain
# rejected by the focused forall_fnset_free_parameter Rust tests.
# Gate: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/atomic/by_known_forall/fnset_free_parameter_carrier.lit
#
# Former failing declaration:
# template<X set>:
#     have selected_functions power_set(fn(x X) X) = {f fn(x X) X: $selected(X, f)}

abstract_prop selected(X, f)
claim:
    ? forall X set:
        {f fn(x X) X: $selected(X, f)} $in power_set(fn(x X) X)
    claim:
        ? forall member {f fn(x X) X: $selected(X, f)}:
            member $in fn(x X) X
    by def:
        ? {f fn(x X) X: $selected(X, f)} $subset fn(x X) X
template<X set>:
    have selected_functions power_set(fn(x X) X) = {f fn(x X) X: $selected(X, f)}
